{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2200-04-03 15:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2200-04-03 15:23:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve been having really bad nausea and vomiting since early this morning. It feels just like my old gastroparesis episodes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2200-04-03 15:24:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any abdominal pain, fever, or diarrhea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2200-04-03 15:25:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no pain or fever. Just the nausea and vomiting. I couldn’t keep anything down, not even water."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2200-04-03 15:26:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. I also see you have type 1 diabetes. How has your blood sugar been?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2200-04-03 15:27:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The night before, it dropped to 38. I ate peanut butter and crackers, but it only went up to 60. I turned off my insulin pump because I was scared of going low again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2200-04-03 15:28:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ll monitor your glucose closely. For now, we’re going to keep you NPO—nothing by mouth—for a few hours to let your stomach settle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2200-04-03 15:29:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, but I’m really worried about my blood sugar going high if I’m not eating and not on the pump."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2200-04-03 15:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a valid concern. We’ll give you IV insulin to keep your levels in check. An endocrine specialist will help manage that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2200-04-03 15:32:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I also took lorazepam at home, and it helped a little with the nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2200-04-03 15:33:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve given you ondansetron and more lorazepam. We’ll continue those as needed. We also started a proton-pump inhibitor in case there’s any irritation from vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2200-04-03 16:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs came back. Your sodium is a bit low at 130, likely from vomiting and not drinking. We’re giving you IV fluids to correct that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2200-04-03 16:16:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2200-04-03 16:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s mild and we’re treating it. You should be fine with the fluids. Your kidney function is okay, so it should correct quickly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2200-04-03 16:18:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2200-04-03 18:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noticed a small amount of coffee-ground material in your vomit earlier. Did you see that too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2200-04-03 18:31:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t notice, but I was pretty out of it. Is that blood?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2200-04-03 18:32:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly a small amount, likely from irritation due to retching. Your hemoglobin is stable, so no active bleeding. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2200-04-03 18:33:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I was dry heaving a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2200-04-04 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your white blood cell count was high last night—15.9—but it’s already coming down. We did a chest X-ray to check for infection, and it’s clear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2200-04-04 08:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it an infection then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2200-04-04 08:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Unlikely. No fever, clean urine, and normal lungs. It’s probably a stress response from the vomiting and high glucose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2200-04-04 08:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. That’s good to hear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2200-04-04 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood sugar was up to 395 this morning with an anion gap of 21. That means you had mild ketoacidosis. But it’s already improving with insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2200-04-04 10:16:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I thought stopping the pump would prevent highs, but I guess not eating made it worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2200-04-04 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Without insulin, even without food, your body makes glucose. We’re glad the gap is closing quickly. No signs of infection or other triggers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2200-04-04 10:19:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad it’s under control now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2200-04-04 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood cultures came back with no growth so far. That’s reassuring—no bloodstream infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2200-04-04 14:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. And my nausea is definitely better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2200-04-04 14:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and your vitals are stabilizing. Heart rate is down from 103 to 88. Your blood pressure was a bit high earlier, so we restarted your lisinopril."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2200-04-04 14:03:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I forgot to ask—was my Port-A-Cath checked? I know it’s there, but I wanted to make sure it’s okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2200-04-04 14:04:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the chest X-ray confirmed it’s in place and unchanged. No complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2200-04-04 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel a lot safer knowing that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2200-04-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news. You’ve gone over 24 hours without vomiting. We’re going to start you on clear liquids and see how you do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2200-04-05 09:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! Can I have some broth?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2200-04-05 09:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start with broth and water. If you tolerate it, we’ll advance to soft foods later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2200-04-05 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well with the liquids. How’s your stomach feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2200-04-05 11:31:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. No nausea at all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2200-04-05 11:32:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’re going to switch you to a soft diet—mashed potatoes, applesauce, things like that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2200-04-05 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your latest labs show your sodium is now 133, and your glucose is 182. Both are much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2200-04-05 15:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Can I go back on my insulin pump?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2200-04-05 15:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to restart it tomorrow morning. The endocrine team approved it since your levels are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2200-04-05 15:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m really relieved. I feel like I’m getting back to normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2200-04-06 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You tolerated a regular diet last night with no issues. We’ve restarted your insulin pump with a basal rate of 0.75 units per hour."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2200-04-06 07:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. My blood sugar this morning was 261—should I be concerned?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2200-04-06 07:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a bit high, but not alarming. It’ll settle as you resume normal eating. Just keep checking your fingersticks as usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2200-04-06 07:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. What about my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2200-04-06 07:04:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re back on lisinopril, amitriptyline, and clonazepam. We’re adding ondansetron for nausea as needed, and docusate and senna for constipation prevention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2200-04-06 07:05:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll take those as directed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2200-04-06 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. We’re planning to discharge you today. Your vitals are stable, and you’re tolerating food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2200-04-06 07:08:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2200-04-06 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Before you leave, let’s go over your discharge instructions. Your nausea was due to gastroparesis, and we managed it with medications and diet advancement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2200-04-06 09:31:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the high blood sugar?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2200-04-06 09:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That was from holding your insulin when you were NPO. Going forward, even if you’re not eating, you still need some insulin. We’ll adjust the pump settings if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2200-04-06 09:33:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll be more careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2200-04-06 09:34:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, keep taking the new meds—ondansetron for nausea, and the stool softeners. Follow up with your primary doctor in a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2200-04-06 09:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2200-04-06 09:37:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re discharging you home in good condition. Call us if you start vomiting again or if your blood sugar goes out of range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2200-04-06 09:38:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I feel much better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2200-04-06 09:39:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Your husband is here, right? He can help you get settled at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2200-04-06 09:40:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, he’s waiting outside. He’s been so supportive."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2200-04-06 09:41:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. Make sure to rest and take it easy for the next few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2200-04-06 09:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2200-04-06 09:44:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2200-04-06 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before you leave—any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2200-04-06 10:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’m all set. Everything’s clear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2200-04-06 10:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Have a safe trip home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2200-04-03 15:22:00",
    "admission_end": "2200-04-06 15:50:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes, gastroparesis, and anxiety was admitted for nausea and vomiting. She developed transient hyponatremia and mild diabetic ketoacidosis after discontinuing her insulin pump due to hypoglycemia. She was managed with IV fluids, insulin, and antiemetics. Her white blood cell count was initially elevated but downtrended without evidence of infection. Her diet was advanced as nausea resolved, and she was restarted on her insulin pump. By discharge, she was tolerating a regular diet, hemodynamically stable, and cleared to return home with medication adjustments and follow-up plans.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Hyposmolality and/or hyponatremia",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Tachycardia, unspecified",
      "Leukocytosis, unspecified",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Insulin pump status"
    ]
  }
}
